#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Pendahuluan {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To solve any utility-scale quantum problem, we will need to move information around on a quantum computer from one qubit to another. There are well-known protocols for doing this, but some of the most foundational were cast in the context of sending information between distant parties. Throughout this lesson, we will sometimes use language consistent with this context, such as \"distant friends sending information\". But keep in mind that these protocols have broader significance in quantum computing. In this lesson we consider the following quantum communication protocols:\n"
"- **Quantum teleportation**\n"
"    Using a shared entangled state (sometimes called an e-bit) to send an unknown quantum state to a distant friend, requiring supplemental classical communication.\n"
"- **Quantum superdense coding**\n"
"    How to send two bits of information by sending a single qubit to a distant friend (again using prior shared entangled qubits).\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menyelesaikan masalah kuantum skala utilitas apa pun, kita perlu memindahkan informasi di dalam komputer kuantum dari satu qubit ke qubit lain. Ada protokol yang sudah dikenal untuk melakukan hal ini, dan beberapa yang paling mendasar dirumuskan dalam konteks pengiriman informasi antar pihak yang berjauhan. Sepanjang pelajaran ini, kita kadang akan menggunakan bahasa yang sesuai dengan konteks ini, seperti \"teman yang berjauhan saling mengirim informasi\". Tapi ingat bahwa protokol ini memiliki makna yang lebih luas dalam komputasi kuantum. Dalam pelajaran ini kita mempertimbangkan protokol komunikasi kuantum berikut:\n"
"- **Teleportasi kuantum**\n"
"    Menggunakan state belitan bersama (kadang disebut e-bit) untuk mengirimkan state kuantum yang tidak diketahui ke teman yang berjauhan, dengan membutuhkan komunikasi klasik tambahan.\n"
"- **Pengkodean superdense kuantum**\n"
"    Cara mengirimkan dua bit informasi hanya dengan mengirimkan satu qubit ke teman yang berjauhan (lagi-lagi menggunakan qubit belitan bersama yang sudah disiapkan sebelumnya).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more background relevant to these topics, we recommend lesson 4 in "
"Basics of Quantum Information on [Entanglement in "
"action](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-"
"action/introduction).\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk latar belakang lebih lanjut yang relevan dengan topik-topik ini, kami "
"merekomendasikan pelajaran 4 dalam Basics of Quantum Information tentang "
"[Entanglement in action](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/introduction).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above description, an \"unknown quantum state\" simply refers to a state of the form described in the previous lesson:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+\\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"where $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are complex numbers such that $|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2 = 1$.  This allows us to write the quantum state as\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle=\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\begin{matrix}\n"
"\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\\n"
"e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{matrix}\n"
"\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
"Since we want to be able to transfer the information in any random quantum state, generating such a state is where we will begin this lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam deskripsi di atas, \"state kuantum yang tidak diketahui\" hanya merujuk pada state berbentuk seperti yang dijelaskan di pelajaran sebelumnya:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+\\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"di mana $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ adalah bilangan kompleks sehingga $|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2 = 1$. Ini memungkinkan kita menuliskan state kuantum sebagai\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle=\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\begin{matrix}\n"
"\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\\n"
"e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{matrix}\n"
"\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
"Karena kita ingin bisa mentransfer informasi dalam state kuantum acak apa pun, membuat state semacam itu adalah titik awal pelajaran ini.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Density matrices {#2-density-matrices}"
msgstr "2. Matriks densitas {#2-density-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also write the quantum state $|\\psi \\rangle$ as its density matrix. This form is useful for denoting probabilistic mixture\n"
"of pure quantum states. In the case of a single qubit, we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga bisa menuliskan state kuantum $|\\psi \\rangle$ sebagai matriks "
"densitasnya. Bentuk ini berguna untuk menyatakan campuran probabilistik dari"
" state kuantum murni. Untuk satu qubit, kita bisa menuliskan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi| \\equiv  \\rho = \\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\\n"
"e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} & e^{-i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\n"
"=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1+\\cos\\theta & e^{-i\\varphi}\\sin\\theta\\\\\n"
"e^{-i\\varphi}\\sin\\theta & 1-\\cos\\theta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi| \\equiv  \\rho = \\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\\n"
"e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} & e^{-i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\n"
"=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1+\\cos\\theta & e^{-i\\varphi}\\sin\\theta\\\\\n"
"e^{-i\\varphi}\\sin\\theta & 1-\\cos\\theta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the density matrix $\\rho$ is a linear summation of Pauli "
"matrices, as below,\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa matriks densitas $\\rho$ adalah penjumlahan linear dari "
"matriks Pauli, seperti di bawah ini,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2}\\bigl( \\textbf{I} + (\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\varphi})\\textbf{X}+  (\\sin{\\theta}\\sin{\\varphi})\\textbf{Y} +  (\\cos{\\theta})\\textbf{Z} \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2}\\bigl( \\textbf{I} + (\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\varphi})\\textbf{X}+  (\\sin{\\theta}\\sin{\\varphi})\\textbf{Y} +  (\\cos{\\theta})\\textbf{Z} \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Or, in general,\n"
msgstr "Atau, secara umum,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2}(\\textbf{I} + r_{x}\\textbf{X}+ r_{y}\\textbf{Y} + r_{z}\\textbf{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2}(\\textbf{I} + r_{x}\\textbf{X}+ r_{y}\\textbf{Y} + r_{z}\\textbf{Z})\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where\n"
"$r_{x}^2+r_{y}^2+r_{z}^2=1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana\n"
"$r_{x}^2+r_{y}^2+r_{z}^2=1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "And, the Bloch vector is $\\textbf{r} = (r_{x}, r_{y}, r_{z})$.\n"
msgstr "Dan, vektor Bloch adalah $\\textbf{r} = (r_{x}, r_{y}, r_{z})$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now, let's make an arbitrary quantum state using random numbers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, mari kita buat state kuantum acak menggunakan bilangan acak.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can show this Bloch vector on the Bloch sphere.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa menampilkan vektor Bloch ini pada bola Bloch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-"
"outputs/2e4d869d-5d0d-4c4b-8cf9-e8e05b423a00-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-"
"outputs/2e4d869d-5d0d-4c4b-8cf9-e8e05b423a00-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Quantum state tomography {#3-quantum-state-tomography}"
msgstr "3. Tomografi state kuantum {#3-quantum-state-tomography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you only measure the quantum state in the computational basis ($|0 "
"\\rangle$ and  $|1 \\rangle$), the phase information (the complex number "
"information) will be lost. But if we have many copies of $|\\psi \\rangle$ "
"by repeating the preparation process (we can't clone states, but we can "
"repeat preparation processes), we can estimate the value of $r_{x}, r_{y}, "
"r_{z}$ by performing *quantum state tomography* for density matrix $\\rho$. "
"Given the form:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kamu hanya mengukur state kuantum dalam basis komputasi ($|0 \\rangle$ "
"dan  $|1 \\rangle$), informasi fase (informasi bilangan kompleks) akan "
"hilang. Tapi jika kita punya banyak salinan $|\\psi \\rangle$ dengan "
"mengulang proses persiapan (kita tidak bisa mengkloning state, tapi kita "
"bisa mengulang proses persiapan), kita bisa memperkirakan nilai $r_{x}, "
"r_{y}, r_{z}$ dengan melakukan *tomografi state kuantum* untuk matriks "
"densitas $\\rho$. Dengan bentuk:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "it holds that\n"
msgstr "berlaku bahwa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Tr(\\textbf{X} \\rho) =  r_{x}, \\quad Tr(\\textbf{Y} \\rho) =  r_{y}, \\quad Tr(\\textbf{Z} \\rho) =  r_{z}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Tr(\\textbf{X} \\rho) =  r_{x}, \\quad Tr(\\textbf{Y} \\rho) =  r_{y}, \\quad Tr(\\textbf{Z} \\rho) =  r_{z}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In $r_{z}$ case,\n"
msgstr "Untuk kasus $r_{z}$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Tr(\\textbf{Z} \\rho) =  \\langle 0|\\textbf{Z} \\rho|0 \\rangle +  \\langle 1|\\textbf{Z} \\rho|1 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle 0|(|0 \\rangle\\langle 0|-|1 \\rangle\\langle 1|) \\rho|0 \\rangle +\\langle 1|(|0 \\rangle\\langle 0|-|1 \\rangle\\langle 1|) \\rho|1 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\langle 0|\\rho|0 \\rangle- \\langle 1| \\rho|1 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\langle 0|\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi|0 \\rangle -  \\langle 1| \\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi|1 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=|\\alpha|^2-|\\beta|^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Tr(\\textbf{Z} \\rho) =  \\langle 0|\\textbf{Z} \\rho|0 \\rangle +  \\langle 1|\\textbf{Z} \\rho|1 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle 0|(|0 \\rangle\\langle 0|-|1 \\rangle\\langle 1|) \\rho|0 \\rangle +\\langle 1|(|0 \\rangle\\langle 0|-|1 \\rangle\\langle 1|) \\rho|1 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\langle 0|\\rho|0 \\rangle- \\langle 1| \\rho|1 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\langle 0|\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi|0 \\rangle -  \\langle 1| \\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi|1 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=|\\alpha|^2-|\\beta|^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last transformation of the equation is for $|\\psi \\rangle  "
"=\\alpha|0\\rangle+\\beta|1\\rangle$. Therefore, we can obtain $r_{z}$ by "
"probability of $|0 \\rangle$  - Probability of $|1 \\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Transformasi terakhir dari persamaan ini berlaku untuk $|\\psi \\rangle  "
"=\\alpha|0\\rangle+\\beta|1\\rangle$. Oleh karena itu, kita bisa mendapatkan"
" $r_{z}$ dari probabilitas $|0 \\rangle$  - Probabilitas $|1 \\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Estimate $r_z$ value {#estimate-r-z-value}"
msgstr "Estimasi nilai $r_z$ {#estimate-r-z-value}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to estimate $r_z$, we create a quantum state and measure it. We "
"then repeat the preparation and measurement many times. Finally we use the "
"statistics of the measurement to estimate the probabilities above and thus "
"estimate $r_z$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengestimasi $r_z$, kita buat state kuantum dan mengukurnya. Kita "
"ulangi persiapan dan pengukuran berkali-kali. Akhirnya kita gunakan "
"statistik pengukuran untuk mengestimasi probabilitas di atas dan dengan "
"demikian mengestimasi $r_z$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For creating the random quantum state, we will use the general unitary gate "
"$U$ with the parameters $ \\theta, \\varphi$. (Refer to "
"[U-gate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.UGate)"
" for more information.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk membuat state kuantum acak, kita akan menggunakan gate unitary umum "
"$U$ dengan parameter $ \\theta, \\varphi$. (Lihat "
"[U-gate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.UGate)"
" untuk informasi lebih lanjut.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-"
"outputs/b1327267-f2fe-4a61-91d9-328c672b557e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-"
"outputs/b1327267-f2fe-4a61-91d9-328c672b557e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the `AerSimulator`, we will measure it in the computational basis to "
"estimate $r_z$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan `AerSimulator`, kita akan mengukurnya dalam basis komputasi "
"untuk mengestimasi $r_z$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-"
"outputs/6d5006d5-6eac-4015-be9d-bd5f01e046b7-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-"
"outputs/6d5006d5-6eac-4015-be9d-bd5f01e046b7-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the quantum state tomography method, we estimated the $r_z$ value. In "
"this case, since we chose a parameter for the \"random\" state, we know the "
"value of $r_z$ and can check our work. But by its very nature, utility-scale"
" work is not always so trivial to check. We will discuss more about checking"
" quantum results later in this course. For now, simply note that our "
"estimation was reasonably accurate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan metode tomografi state kuantum, kita mengestimasi nilai $r_z$. "
"Dalam hal ini, karena kita memilih parameter untuk state \"acak\", kita "
"mengetahui nilai $r_z$ dan bisa memeriksa pekerjaan kita. Tapi pada "
"hakikatnya, pekerjaan skala utilitas tidak selalu semudah itu untuk "
"diperiksa. Kita akan membahas lebih lanjut tentang memeriksa hasil kuantum "
"nanti dalam kursus ini. Untuk sekarang, cukup perhatikan bahwa estimasi kita"
" cukup akurat.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Exercise 1: Estimate $r_x$ value {#exercise-1-estimate-r-x-value}"
msgstr "Latihan 1: Estimasi nilai $r_x$ {#exercise-1-estimate-r-x-value}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that IBM&reg; quantum computers measure along the $z$-axis (sometimes"
" stated \"in the $z$ basis\" or \"in the computational basis\"). However, by"
" using rotations before the measurement, we can measure the quantum state's "
"projection on the x-axis, also. To be more precise, if we rotate our system "
"such that things that did point along $x$ now point along $z$, then we can "
"keep the same measurement hardware along $z$, but learn about the state that"
" was just along $x$ a moment ago. This is how most quantum computers (and "
"all IBM quantum computers) perform measurements along multiple axes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahwa komputer kuantum IBM&reg; mengukur sepanjang sumbu $z$ (kadang "
"dinyatakan \"dalam basis $z$\" atau \"dalam basis komputasi\"). Namun, "
"dengan menggunakan rotasi sebelum pengukuran, kita juga bisa mengukur "
"proyeksi state kuantum pada sumbu x. Lebih tepatnya, jika kita memutar "
"sistem kita sehingga hal-hal yang semula menunjuk ke arah $x$ kini menunjuk "
"ke arah $z$, maka kita bisa tetap menggunakan hardware pengukuran yang sama "
"sepanjang $z$, tapi belajar tentang state yang baru saja berada di sepanjang"
" $x$ sesaat yang lalu. Inilah cara sebagian besar komputer kuantum (dan "
"semua komputer kuantum IBM) melakukan pengukuran sepanjang beberapa sumbu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this understanding, try writing code to estimate the value of $r_x,$ "
"using quantum state tomography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan pemahaman ini, coba tulis kode untuk mengestimasi nilai $r_x,$ "
"menggunakan tomografi state kuantum.\n"

